From eaab93260fdea60e665f850af74c7a12710bb73e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 17:30:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/49] Round the search engine icon in the omnibox

The search engine icon is a square bitmap with a white background. The new tab page clipped
it to a circle, the omnibox did not, so the icon changed shape when moving between the two.

StatusView had all the machinery for this already. It holds a RoundedCornerOutlineProvider,
keeps its radius current through setCornerRadiusRes, and enables clipping with
setClipToOutline. What it never did was attach the provider to the view, so clipping fell
back to the default outline provider, which is the rectangular bounds of the view. The clip
therefore did nothing and the provider was dead code.

Attaching it fixes the shape and also revives the radius switching in StatusMediator, which
moves between a 4dp and a 12dp radius on focus and had no effect for the same reason.
---
 .../chrome/browser/omnibox/status/StatusView.java        | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/android/omnibox/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/omnibox/status/StatusView.java b/chrome/browser/ui/android/omnibox/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/omnibox/status/StatusView.java
index 0b9c29f01c..68852a2cef 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/android/omnibox/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/omnibox/status/StatusView.java
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/android/omnibox/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/omnibox/status/StatusView.java
@@ -145,6 +145,15 @@ public class StatusView extends LinearLayout {
                 getResources()
                         .getDimensionPixelSize(R.dimen.omnibox_search_engine_logo_composed_size);
         setCornerRadiusRes(R.dimen.omnibox_search_engine_logo_composed_half_size);
+        // De-Googled build: attach the rounding provider before clipping.
+        //
+        // setClipToOutline(true) on its own clips to the default outline provider, which is the
+        // view's rectangular bounds, so the clip did nothing and mIconCornerRadiusProvider was
+        // built and kept up to date by setCornerRadiusRes() without ever being used. The search
+        // engine icon is a square bitmap with a white background, so it rendered as a white
+        // square in the omnibox while the new tab page, which does attach its provider, drew the
+        // same icon as a circle.
+        mIconView.setOutlineProvider(mIconCornerRadiusProvider);
         mIconView.setClipToOutline(true);
 
         configureAccessibilityDescriptions();
